The call rules, exactly: a CALL is an occurrence of the symbol in operator
position — the first element of a compound form — resolved through the file's
package context (in-package, package prefixes, local nicknames). #'x and 'x
are references, not calls; comments and strings never count; a symbol's own
definition form is not a call. Load order for package creation: kernel,
ledger, actor, tools, cli.

Grading runs against a pristine copy of these files plus your answer.txt, so
editing the sources changes nothing.
